.org/threads/oral-castor-oil.1629569/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251115220431/https://looksmax.org/threads/oral-castor-oil.1629569/"},{"title":"how to use castor oil and its benefits for hair","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/how-to-use-castor-oil-and-its-benefits-for-hair.1589451/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250914120751/https://looksmax.org/threads/how-to-use-castor-oil-and-its-benefits-for-hair.1589451/"},{"title":"oral castor oil question","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/oral-castor-oil-question.1581884/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251018164056/https://looksmax.org/threads/oral-castor-oil-question.1581884/"},{"title":"is castor oil cope or should i slap it on my eyebrows and goattee","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/is-castor-oil-cope-or-should-i-slap-it-on-my-eyebrows-and-goattee.1575112/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251018100035/https://looksmax.org/threads/is-castor-oil-cope-or-should-i-slap-it-on-my-eyebrows-and-goattee.1575112/"},{"title":"minoxidil and castor oil","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/minoxidil-and-castor-oil.1492034/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250916065112/https://looksmax.org/threads/minoxidil-and-castor-oil.1492034/"},{"title":"is castor oil cope","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/is-castor-oil-cope.1372281/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250403081957/https://looksmax.org/threads/is-castor-oil-cope.1372281/"},{"title":"1 months eyelash transformation on castor oil","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/1-months-eyelash-transformation-on-castor-oil.1223237/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251012030024/https://looksmax.org/threads/1-months-eyelash-transformation-on-castor-oil.1223237/"},{"title":"topical or oral castor oil","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/topical-or-oral-castor-oil.1027984/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240519112202/https://looksmax.org/threads/topical-or-oral-castor-oil.1027984/"},{"title":"oral minox vs oral castor oil","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/oral-minox-vs-oral-castor-oil.951242/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240318113050/https://looksmax.org/threads/oral-minox-vs-oral-castor-oil.951242/"},{"title":"gonna start using rosemary and castor oil for eyebrows and eyelashes any tips","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/gonna-start-using-rosemary-and-castor-oil-for-eyebrows-and-eyelashes-any-tips.941624/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240318112523/https://looksmax.org/threads/gonna-start-using-rosemary-and-castor-oil-for-eyebrows-and-eyelashes-any-tips.941624/"}],"web":[{"title":"Castor oil — Grokipedia","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Castor_oil"},{"title":"Castor oil - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castor_oil"},{"title":"Hair conditioner - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hair_conditioner"}]},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Castor_oil","lead":["Castor oil is a thick, pale vegetable oil pressed from the seeds of the castor plant, Ricinus communis. About 90 percent of its fatty acids are ricinoleates [1]. It has been used for centuries as a laxative and today also serves as an industrial raw material and cosmetic ingredient [1][2].","In looksmaxxing communities it is discussed mainly as a topical oil applied to hair, eyebrows and eyelashes, where proponents say it thickens growth. The Wikipedia article on castor oil makes no hair claims, and no clinical trial of castor oil for hair growth appears in the sources reviewed [1].","Its established medical use is oral, as a stimulant laxative; the US label for an over-the-counter product lists temporary relief of occasional constipation [3]."],"infobox":[["Source","Seeds of Ricinus communis"],["Main component","Ricinoleic acid (about 90% of fatty acids) [1]"],["Established uses","Laxative, emollient, industrial lubricant and polymer feedstock [1]"],["Earliest recorded medical use","Ebers Papyrus, c. 1550 BC [1]"],["Legal status","Sold over the counter as a laxative and cosmetic ingredient (US)"]],"sections":[{"h":"Uses","paras":[],"subs":[{"h":"Medical and industrial uses","paras":["Castor oil is recorded as a laxative in the Ebers Papyrus, dated about 1550 BC [1]. Industrially it goes into polyurethanes, coatings, lubricants and biodiesel, and food-grade forms appear as additives [1][2]. It is also a vehicle for some injected medicines [1]. For labour induction, a systematic review of three trials (233 women) reported insufficient evidence of benefit, and all women taking it orally felt nauseous [1]."]},{"h":"Cosmetic and hair uses","paras":["Cosmetically it acts as an emollient and carrier in products such as lipsticks and hair conditioners [4]. Wikipedia's overview of hair conditioners notes that natural oils have been used to condition hair for centuries, and that modern products have largely replaced simple oils with silicones, fatty alcohols and polymers [5]. Castor oil is not named in that overview [5]. Online, people apply it to scalp, beard, brows and lashes, usually with a brush or fingers."]}]},{"h":"Safety and adverse effects","paras":["Taken by mouth, castor oil commonly causes nausea, vomiting and diarrhoea, and medical guidance discourages its use for simple constipation [1]. The US label advises against use when abdominal pain, nausea or vomiting are present unless directed by a doctor [3]. Castor beans contain ricin, but ricin is not present in the processed oil [1][4]. A pregnancy drug reference advises against oral or topical use in women who are pre-term pregnant [1]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Chemistry and production","paras":["Seeds contain roughly 30 to 60 percent oil depending on source, and the oil is obtained by pressing or solvent extraction [1][4]. Its distinctive hydroxylated fatty acid, ricinoleic acid, gives it high viscosity and lubricity [4][2]. India is the largest producer [4]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Use in looksmaxxing communities","paras":["On looksmax.org, castor oil is most often discussed for eyebrows and eyelashes, sometimes combined with rosemary oil, minoxidil or derma stamping. Reports are mixed: one user described a month of nightly use followed by visibly longer lashes and a friend noticing thicker brows [6], while others report barely noticeable changes after a year [7]. A third thread acknowledges no strong evidence while suggesting it may at least coat brows like mascara [8]. Users also describe its thickness as awkward to apply [6]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found. Registered clinical trials listed for castor oil concern labour induction and dental pulp response, not hair or lash growth. Wikipedia's overview of hair conditioners reports no hair-growth evidence for castor oil [5]."],"subs":[]}],"lore":{"intro":"Castor oil appears repeatedly in hair, brow and lash threads on looksmax.org as a cheap topical growth aid, often debated as to whether it is effective or 'cope'. [7][8]","claims":[{"claim":"Castor oil thickens brows and lengthens lashes.","verdict":"unknown","note":""},{"claim":"Castor oil barely works compared with other options.","verdict":"unknown","note":""},{"claim":"It is harmless even if the effect is unproven, since it coats hair like mascara.","verdict":"unknown","note":""}]},"timeline":[{"year":"c. 1550 BC","event":"Ebers Papyrus records castor oil as a laxative. [1]"}],"refs":[{"title":"Castor oil (Wikipedia)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castor_oil","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Castor oil: a vital industrial raw material","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15919203/","source":"Bioresource Technology","year":2006,"type":"review"},{"title":"US drug label: Castor oil (oral)","url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=004d1dc2-47c1-84d1-e063-6394a90a2471","source":"DailyMed","year":2024,"type":"label"},{"title":"Castor oil (Grokipedia)","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Castor_oil","source":"Grokipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Hair conditioner (Wikipedia)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hair_conditioner","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Castor oil is not cope","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil-is-not-cope.1760243/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2025,"type":"forum"},{"title":"Castor oil on eyebrows/lashes","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil-on-eyebrows-lashes.1768759/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2025,"type":"forum"},{"title":"castor oil + rosemary oil cope?","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil-rosemary-oil-cope.1767452/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2025,"type":"forum"}],"studies":[{"title":"Hair conditioner (Wikipedia)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hair_conditioner","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"kind":null}],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Castor oil on eyebrows/lashes","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil-on-eyebrows-lashes.1768759/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251218000750/https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil-on-eyebrows-lashes.1768759/"},{"title":"castor oil + rosemary oil cope?","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil-rosemary-oil-cope.1767452/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251218164542/https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil-rosemary-oil-cope.1767452/"},{"title":"Castor oil is not cope","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil-is-not-cope.1760243/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251218013136/https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil-is-not-cope.1760243/"},{"title":"castor oil","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil.1758725/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251228112022/https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil.1758725/"},{"title":"castor oil","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil.1753885/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260113184355/https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil.1753885/"},{"title":"castor oil for eyelashes","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil-for-eyelashes.1736346/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251218075240/https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil-for-eyelashes.1736346/"},{"title":"castor oil ricinus oil","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil-ricinus-oil.1698278/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260103054047/https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil-ricinus-oil.1698278/"},{"title":"castor oil for styling","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil-for-styling.1548208/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251014162021/https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil-for-styling.1548208/"},{"title":"castor oil the most misunderstood looksmax and why minoxidil sucks","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil-the-most-misunderstood-looksmax-and-why-minoxidil-sucks.1504437/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250630230822/https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil-the-most-misunderstood-looksmax-and-why-minoxidil-sucks.1504437/"},{"title":"castor oil","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil.1467142/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250915070348/https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil.1467142/"},{"title":"castor oil and derma stamping","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil-and-derma-stamping.1467105/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250916073415/https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil-and-derma-stamping.1467105/"},{"title":"castor oil minoxdil","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/castor-oil-minoxdil.1014551/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.ar